      "span": "During analysis, an annotated Arabic corpus is used to extract the required lexical features of the document words.",
      "roles": ["dataset"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A3",
      "span": "The knowledge also includes syntactic rules based on part of speech tags and allowed word sequences to extract the candidate keyphrases.",
      "roles": ["method"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A4",
      "span": "In this work, the abstract form of Arabic words is used instead of its stem form to represent the candidate terms.",
      "roles": ["method"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A5",
      "span": "The Abstract form hides most of the inflections found in Arabic words.",
      "roles": ["contribution"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A6",
      "span": "The paper introduces new features of keyphrases based on linguistic knowledge, to capture titles and subtitles of a document.",
      "roles": ["contribution"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A7",
      "span": "A simple ANOVA test is used to evaluate the validity of selected features.",
      "roles": ["method"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A8",
      "span": "Then, the learning model is built using the LDA - Linear Discriminant Analysis - and training documents.",
      "roles": ["method"],
      "origin": "current"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "A9",
      "span": "Although, the presented system is trained using documents in the IT domain, experiments carried out show that it has a significantly better performance than the existing Arabic extractor systems, where precision and recall values reach double their corresponding values in the other systems especially for lengthy and non-scientific articles.",
      "roles": ["contribution"],
      "origin": "current"
    }
  ]
}

